  "details": "This is a very niche request. If there is a way to override a local video player with a webcam source like OBS virtual camera, this would help tremendously when working with systems like VRSL that rely on control pixels from a stream on the video player.\n\nCurrently, to control these systems, you have to stream your feed into the world via VRCDN or your own media server to control these systems. The difficulty with this is that there will always be a delay with streaming before it reaches the world's video player, making it difficult to control/program these systems. Being able to override the video player stream with a webcam input would allow the systems to be controlled in real-time for the person operating it, eliminating the inconsistent delays with streaming it into the world.\n\nThis would be a feature only local to the user, and the feed could not be seen by anyone else. There could be other alternatives like Spout or NDI, but those may require more in-depth setup or licensing fees, while a webcam source from OBS would be a more straightforward setup.",
